From b600d6ba0f9e22a8c1e12840fe9a2244ea34a153 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:33:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 0020: make the screen answer whether Apple took the card

0019 prints what this kext decided; it cannot say whether the decision was
enough. Publishing LoadAccelerator only makes the card eligible - Apple's
personality still has to match, attach, and reach the end of its own start().
On a machine with no keyboard, that question had no answer at all.

The positive signal already exists: GraphicsAccelerator::start() announces
itself over SpecialAMDKey (type 0x00), and Navi48AccelPeer handles it. The mark
is recorded there before the enable that follows can fail. The negative signal
needs a watcher, so accel_takeover.cpp starts a kernel_thread_start poller that
sleeps in one-second steps for 20 s and stands down the moment the flag lands;
only the miss prints "NO TAKEOVER ... personality did not match this device id".

accel_takeover_report.h owns the rule that keeps that sentence honest: it arms
only when the report was requested AND LoadAccelerator actually went up, so a
closed gate is never blamed on the personality. The positive block is held from
the poller's thread, never Apple's, so start() is not stalled.

accel_takeover_report_test: 73 checks. accel_takeover_report_plant.sh: 41
plants, all caught. Cross-build: 80 objects, 7,249,248 B, MH_KEXT_BUNDLE, no
undefined symbols.
